   "line": [
    "f4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The pawn to f4 — the Four Pawns Attack, objectively one of the very best tries against the Alekhine. If White knows the follow-up, White is simply better, and the pressure is immediate.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "The Four Pawns is the most testing anti-Alekhine — a genuine attempt at an opening advantage, not just a gambit.",
   "plans": "Hold the giant centre and develop into the attack."
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 113.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/ppp1pppp/1n6/4p3/2PP1P2/8/PP4PP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "dxe5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 124,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/ppp1pppp/1n6/4P3/2PP4/8/PP4PP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "fxe5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Recapture toward the centre with the f-pawn — NOT with the d-pawn, which would invite an unfavourable queen trade. The plus of the whole system is a monster centre; the minus is lagging development, so precision is required.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Recapture toward the centre to keep the pawn mass and avoid a queen trade that relieves the defender.",
   "plans": "Complete the centre, then catch up in development."
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 129.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/ppp1pppp/1nn5/4P3/2PP4/8/PP4PP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 1 7",
   "line": [
    "Nc6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 170,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/ppp1pppp/1nn5/4P3/2PP4/4B3/PP4PP/RN1QKBNR b KQkq - 2 7",
   "line": [
    "Be3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Restraint again: the knight to f3 would allow the bishop pin on g4 with heavy pressure on the centre, and the pawn to d5 would simply drop e5. The bishop to e3 is the sound way to defend the pawn.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Defend the centre with a developing move that avoids the pin — the bishop to e3.",
   "plans": "Develop the queen's knight, then the king's knight when safe."
  },
