   "line": [
    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The key reactive break: once the pawn goes to a5, the knight on b6 has lost a pawn's support — so the pawn to d5 strikes, forcing that knight to move and clearing a path for the passed d-pawn.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "When a flank pawn push loosens a piece, a central break can exploit the lost support with tempo.",
   "plans": "Advance the d-pawn and open lines for the pieces."
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 463,
   "fen": "r2q1rk1/1pp1bppp/1n2p3/p2PPb2/1nP5/2N1BN2/PP2B1PP/R2Q1RK1 w - - 1 13",
